{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GYvPBrh7EdzGjDZMbB2zYy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source code, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity against GNU reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `docs/` (specs), `cmd/` (utility implementations), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (platform syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `magefiles/` (build targets, excluded from generation).\n\n**Current state**: Source code exists on the working branch for `pkg/format/` (color.go, column.go, size.go + color_test.go), `pkg/sys/` (fileinfo.go + platform files), and `pkg/testutils/` (difftest.go + difftest_test.go). No `cmd/` implementations exist on this branch. Specs are complete for releases 00.0 through 04.1; code generation has not run for any of them.\n\n**Current release**: rel00.0 (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure). Use cases: uc001-magefiles (excluded from generation per DD7, except cmd/version), uc002-format (code exists, partial tests), uc003-sys (code exists, no tests visible), uc004-testutils (code and tests exist).\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nrel00.0 is the earliest incomplete release. The implementation code for `pkg/format` exists but test coverage is incomplete — `color_test.go` exists but `column_test.go` and `size_test.go` do not appear in source_code. Following canonical ordering (tests after implementation, alphabetical tie-breaking on file path), `column_test.go` (prd003 R1.1–R1.4) is the next task.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd003 R1.1-R1.4: Tests for pkg/format column layout\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd003-format.yaml (R1.1-R1.4 column layout requirements)\n      - pkg/format/column.go (implementation under test -- Columns, PadRight, PadLeft, displayWidth)\n      - pkg/format/color_test.go (test conventions -- package format_test, table-driven subtests, t.Parallel)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/column_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Unit tests for Columns, PadRight, PadLeft, and displayWidth\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test Columns function distributes entries in row-major order into the maximum number of columns that fit within termWidth per prd003 R1.1 and R1.4\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test PadRight and PadLeft pad strings to specified display width with trailing or leading spaces per prd003 R1.2\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test displayWidth returns rune count not byte count for multi-byte UTF-8 strings per prd003 R1.3\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Test Columns edge cases: empty slice returns nil, single entry returns single-column grid, entries exactly filling terminal width\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use external test package format_test matching the convention established in color_test.go\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use table-driven subtests with t.Run matching the pattern in color_test.go\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Column gap constant is 2 (defined in column.go as columnGap); test expectations must account for 2-space inter-column gaps\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"column_test.go compiles and all tests pass with go test ./pkg/format/...\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Columns is tested with 0, 1, and multiple entries across narrow and wide terminal widths including single-column fallback\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"PadRight and PadLeft are each tested with target width shorter than, equal to, and longer than the input display width\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"displayWidth is tested with ASCII strings and multi-byte UTF-8 strings to confirm rune-based counting\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33087,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33087},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac29c38a-bf9a-4580-8808-c7e1fa376f63","uuid":"471c5fba-0aeb-45ca-94b9-9f261966095c"}
